WHAT MEM UNDERSTOOD
The examples support a compact deterministic scheme: normalize the company name, select a mnemonic base by word count, and append share-class or preferred suffixes when present. These are synthetic design rules only, not claims about official market tickers.

[1;38;2;138;173;244mRULE 01 · When generating a synthetic ticker, first remove a leading article such as “The,” discard legal-form suffixes such as Inc., LLC, Ltd., PLC, Corp., or Corporation, and ignore connectors such as “&” when selecting ticker characters; preserve meaningful numeric tokens.[0m
[38;2;202;211;245m  SUPPORT · m000001, m000002, m000003, m000004, m000005, m000006, m000008, m000009, m000010, m000018, m000020[0m
[38;2;202;211;245m  BOUNDARY · none[0m
  GOAL · YES
  WHY · Examples omit leading “The,” legal forms, and “&,” while retaining 7, 3, and 5th as meaningful numeric elements.

[1;38;2;138;173;244mRULE 02 · When the normalized company name has two or more meaningful words, form the base ticker from the initial character of each meaningful word, using the numeric character for a number-bearing word; preserve a meaningful abbreviation such as “AI” as a single ticker component.[0m
[38;2;202;211;245m  SUPPORT · m000001, m000002, m000003, m000004, m000005, m000006, m000007, m000008, m000009, m000010, m000014, m000018, m000019, m000020[0m
[38;2;202;211;245m  BOUNDARY · m000011, m000012, m000013[0m
  GOAL · YES
  WHY · The multiword examples consistently use word initials, including numeric-leading names and the preserved AI abbreviation.

[1;38;2;138;173;244mRULE 03 · When the normalized company name is a single word, derive a concise three-letter mnemonic from that word rather than applying the multiword-initial rule.[0m
[38;2;202;211;245m  SUPPORT · m000011, m000012, m000013[0m
[38;2;202;211;245m  BOUNDARY · m000001, m000002, m000003, m000004, m000005, m000006, m000007, m000008, m000009, m000010, m000014, m000018, m000019, m000020[0m
  GOAL · YES
  WHY · The single-word examples use RED, MER, and SOL, showing a distinct three-letter mnemonic convention; the examples do not establish a unique algorithm for every possible word.

[1;38;2;138;173;244mRULE 04 · When share-class details are present, keep the ordinary company base ticker and append a dot suffix: “.A” or “.B” for the corresponding class and “.P” for Preferred.[0m
[38;2;202;211;245m  SUPPORT · m000015, m000016, m000017[0m
[38;2;202;211;245m  BOUNDARY · m000001, m000002[0m
  GOAL · YES
  WHY · North Star Energy retains NSE for Classes A and B, and Blue River Holdings retains BRH for Preferred, with only the suffix changing.

